Author:     cowork-agent <jonathan.m.farnsworth@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Aug 3 10:56:42 2026 -0700
Commit:     cowork-agent <jonathan.m.farnsworth@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Mon Aug 3 10:56:42 2026 -0700

    ci: give full-tests a trigger that actually fires (push never does)
    
    The post-merge tripwire added in #2188 has never run and never would have.
    `push: branches: [main]` does not fire on this repo's normal merge path:
    auto-enroll-merge.yml enrols each PR with the repo's GITHUB_TOKEN, so GitHub
    performs the merge as `app/github-actions`, and events raised by GITHUB_TOKEN
    do not start workflow runs (AGENTS.md hard rule 14).
    
    Measured: of the last 6 merges, the 5 performed by the app produced ZERO push
    runs; only #2191, merged by a human PAT, produced one. Every run on main in the
    last 24h was `schedule` or `workflow_run`.
    
    That made the 47 files excluded from the required subset uncovered rather than
    deferred, and made the previous commit's "still gated by full-tests" false.
    
    Adds `schedule:` — the trigger empirically proven to fire here — and documents
    it honestly as best-effort: release-reconcile declares every-15-min and actually
    fired 16 times in 24h, a 6x shortfall with a 3h47m gap. Good enough for a
    tripwire, explicitly not good enough for a gate, which is why required-tests
    stays on `pull_request`.
    
    tests/test_tests_workflow.py pins this and the earlier concurrency fix as
    invariants, so a regression fails a test instead of silently going quiet.
    Mutation-probed: removing the schedule trigger turns it red.
    
    Not fixed here, and deliberately: build-image.yml has the same dead push:main
    trigger, but release-reconcile.yml's path-aware drift check already covers it
    (last decision: "in sync — deploy 64f27fe7 contains 64f27fe7").

